  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. One encounter, from input 7, against both shrine guardians at once. Input 2 mentions a horse that does not exist, to test PHANTOM detection. Input 6 grants advantage because the candle lights the shrine. Sefa's mace is weak, so most of her damage comes from Fire Bolt, a cantrip: narration of Fire Bolt using up magic is a RESOURCE divergence. Cure Wounds at inputs 12 and 20 spends two of her three slots, so one is left at the end. Input 19 is a narration-only turn that invites a hit-point band phrase about Sefa. Inputs 7 to 18 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; extra ones are rejected and do not advance the game."
